post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
AuraScan installed.

Run first-run setup:
  aurascan init

Check local configuration:
  aurascan doctor

Run aurascan init to optionally enable read-only incident monitoring, the unprivileged Agent Instruction Guard, logged-in AI assistants, and the separately controlled reversible Safe Autopilot policy; Agent Instruction Guard monitoring and its separate AI assistant remain disabled until you opt in.
Run aurascan init or aurascan recovery --install to explicitly install the optional recovery image and boot entry; package installation leaves them disabled.

For AUR build-time protection, configure your helper to use:
  aurascan-makepkg
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
AuraScan upgraded.

Review setup and local diagnostics when needed:
  aurascan init
  aurascan doctor

Run aurascan init to review optional incident and Agent Instruction Guard monitoring, their separate background AI settings, and Safe Autopilot policy.
Run aurascan recovery --status to check an enabled recovery image after major kernel or storage changes.

For AUR build-time protection, configure your helper to use:
  aurascan-makepkg
EOF
}
